fuxi: 0120 -- name the halt/restart, and make the fb command visible

Something resets this phone 30-90 s into every boot with no panic in the ring.  The
one path that reboots without a panic is PEHaltRestartInternal(): it asks IOKit PM
clients to shut down, waits kShutdownTimeout (30 s) and then panics with
"Halt/Restart Timed Out" -- which matches the observed lag exactly.  It now logs the
type, the details and its callers, and the timeout callback says so before panicking.

Also prints "FUXI FB: cmd fb scale N" when a capture is requested, so the live stream
proves whether the command reached the kernel at all.  The screen grab has produced no
frames and no log line; without this print there is no way to tell a lost command from
a failed capture.

Diagnostic only.

Harness: applied=119 skipped=0.
